# mix-of-capabilities 04×23 (4) — la lacuna nomina il sintagma, non la prima parola
# ignota. «what does a carbon monoxide detector detect?» costruiva la lacuna su
# «monoxide» e la rete leggeva «Oxide». `turn_gap_phrase/2` (grammar.p0) deriva il
# nome dopo il determinante, fino al verbo; col «do» ausiliare il verbo nudo in coda
# si toglie. La pagina locale e' il testo di tests/fixtures/wiki.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the gap names the compound noun of the turn]
!timeout 30
> what does a radon detector detect?
<~ radon detector
<! about detector
> what does a carbon monoxide alarm detect?
<~ carbon monoxide alarm
<! about monoxide

[test the bare verb at the end of a do-question is not part of the name]
!timeout 30
> what does a glimpwort need?
<! glimpwort need

[test yes reads the page of the whole name]
!timeout 30
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> what does a programmable logic controller control?
<~ programmable logic controller
> yes
<~ Looking up programmable logic controller
